NEG-only progress activation
============================

Purpose and scope
-----------------

This entry publishes the administrative consequences of one already published,
independently reviewed typed NEG batch. It proves no group-theoretic statement.
The accepted ledger and its mathematical applications supply those statements.
The entry reads status bytes and metadata; Original matrices, permutations,
forests, point sets, witnesses and their values remain opaque. No scientific
worker is launched. A new mathematical manuscript, conjecture, Lean theorem or
compression measurement receives no credit.

The source descends from the accepted seven-fact progress updater
``progress/stages/reviewed_direct_and_invariant_unions/update.py``. The old
publication order, beforeimages, cache-bank append, input closing checks and
sole-writer CAS discipline are reused. This successor removes its hardcoded
indices, prefix, cache size, counts and stage. The old whole-runtime JSON
conversion is replaced by the literal lexical parser from the reviewed F009
administrative checker. Unknown object values and scientific payload spans are
copied as bytes. The shared 3744-byte metadata reader is unchanged.

There is no claim that this is a literal copy of the whole old updater. Source
ancestry and the complete textual difference are shipped separately. There is
also no claim of novelty for NEG bookkeeping, serialization, CAS, or the reused
mathematical applications.

Roles and actual invocations
----------------------------

The author prepares Source and FALSE templates only. A distinct reviewer must
read the complete current Source, helper, manifests and this protocol and issue
``SUPPORTED_STATIC_L026_NEG_ACTIVATION_SOURCE`` with no blockers. The peer names
exact ``program``, ``Source_manifest``, ``protocol``, ``controls_program`` and
``controls_Source_manifest`` descriptors. Root must independently own the whole
current Source and protocol. A positive template or an author assertion is not
an actual invocation.

Before an operational entry, Root executes the fresh synthetic controls under
the reviewed validation supervisor. A distinct actual-controls leaf must name
program, Source_manifest and controls_Source_manifest; status must begin
SUPPORTED_ACTUAL, blockers must be empty, count must equal the number of unique
control_names, Original_payloads_decoded must be false, and
actual_guard_and_raw_frames_verified must be true. Old ledger-writer controls
remain attributed to their own writer; they are not retagged as these controls.

All actual commands use actor /root. The controls and operational children use
Python -EBS with no optimization. The retained validation supervisor uses
Python -EB, preserving its psutil dependency. The five Python environment
overrides are removed from the complete invocation.
The guard admits at most 256 MiB RSS and 125 seconds, with a cooperative
115-second input interval. The actual receipt, raw frames and SDK are retained
by Root; no command in the templates has been run by the author. Validation
input floors and project-lock admission remain those of the existing guard.

Prepare
-------

CLI::

  activate.py --actor /root --mode prepare \
    --Root-request PATH BYTES SHA256 --Source-peer PATH BYTES SHA256

Root issues one immutable ROOT_L026_NEG_ACTIVATION_PREPARATION_V1 request. It
binds current Source, protocol, distinct Source peer, actual controls and a
fresh independently reviewed published-ledger postwrite leaf. Its exact
snapshot is the current intake/controller/runtime triple. Root owns the sole
canonical-writer window and states that no current-prefix forest cohort is
active. The entry independently refuses any cohort.json at that prefix.

The postwrite leaf has the old d098 activation fields: publication_verified and
Root_canonical_write_issued true; canonical.current/receipt/bank/batch; counts;
registered_total; new_NEG, new_GEN and new_IP; exact_changes and
exact_status_changes; plan; Root_release; historical_mutable_input_aliases.
Original_payloads_decoded must be false. This is a leaf for the new published
ledger, not a retrospective invention of a numerical or mathematical run.

The source verifies both complete 28,908-byte status banks. Between one and
sixteen distinct sorted rows change from 0 to 1. No other status byte changes.
Every new fact is NEG. GEN and separate IP are unchanged. The receipt, batch,
Root writer release, method descriptors, original scope and predecessor agree.
The old mutable CURRENT is read only through an exact retained alias; its
original descriptor is not falsely loaded from the replaced live path. The
inverse of the new CURRENT must recover that old alias up to lexical JSON
structure and primitive tokens.

Current progress counters must agree with the old bank. Current F009 prefix
and all three count joins are obtained dynamically, and strict slots equal
156 times that prefix. Both intake and runtime must retain 101 complete of
104 mathematical originals. Measurement coverage remains 53 applications and
19 topics. The entry reads every old cache-bank body opaquely, checks its
announced keys and disjointness, and refuses a duplicate new key.

Prepare writes a fresh private directory under this package's plans directory.
It does not create the final progress stage or replace a live pointer. Its
complete images are old intake/controller/runtime, new intake/controller/runtime,
new one-entry cache bank, and a copy of the exact current Source. All public
progress references inside those private images name the eventual final stage.
A private plan records both physical private descriptors and final descriptors,
all input pins, the snapshot, counts and the inverse. The preparation timestamp
is fixed once and is reused unchanged during application.

A distinct actual-plan review must bind exact plan, program, Source_manifest
and snapshot, set whole_afterimages_and_typed_preservation_verified and
actual_guard_and_raw_frames_verified true, and disclose its finite scope.
The reviewer checks whole private bodies and inverse, every old cache value,
all protected and unknown fields, and genuine Root invocation provenance.
This review is not a second proof of the borrowed mathematics.

Apply
-----

CLI::

  activate.py --actor /root --mode apply \
    --Root-request PATH BYTES SHA256 --Source-peer PATH BYTES SHA256 \
    --plan PATH BYTES SHA256 --plan-review PATH BYTES SHA256 \
    --Root-decision PATH BYTES SHA256

Root issues a separate ROOT_L026_NEG_ACTIVATION_APPLY_V1 decision after reading
the complete private images and independent actual-plan review. It binds all
current Source, request, snapshot, plan and review descriptors. No FALSE template
grants publication authority.

Apply repeats the complete semantic and raw-span checks, the exact input pins,
the dynamic prefix freeze, and the current three-way snapshot. It regenerates
all expected bytes from the held beforeimages, exact new batch and retained
preparation timestamp and requires exact equality with all private images.
All reads close before publication. It writes and hashes a fresh immutable
stage, then compares the live intake/controller to the exact original snapshot.
Controller is replaced first; intake is replaced last after another intake CAS.
Temporary files and parent directories are fsynced. The runtime target is an
immutable stage image rather than a mutable runtime pointer.

A live partial publication is possible if a process or filesystem fails between
these replacements. No process lock, simultaneous multi-file transaction or
race-free CAS is claimed. Root owns serialization. A partial failure requires
metadata reconciliation from exact before/after images and actual frames;
it never authorizes scientific replay. An occupied stage or private path is
refused rather than reused or overwritten.

The final readback pins the live pointers and new stage files and explicitly
leaves independent administrative adoption and its own operational-tail
retention pending. No full manuscript is credited.

Preservation and bounds
-----------------------

All old inline cache value bytes and old bank descriptor spans are unchanged.
Every old bank body is whole-hashed. Only one fresh cache-bank descriptor and
one new typed-batch cache value are added. F004, F009, public state, intake,
measurement coverage and all unknown fields retain their exact value spans.
Within L026 only paid/generation/proper/subset_NEG/separate_IP/unpaid/
bank_unresolved/current_typed_ledger/negative_progress_activation/next change.
Within runtime only the five L026 count fields and explicit L026 method,
snapshot, cache-bank, activation and checkpoint fields change. GEN and IP
numeric values are also checked unchanged. Whole-document formatting outside
value spans may normalize, but preserved scientific values are never decoded.

Every file is at most 4 MiB, input path limit is 512, total tracked plus nominal
Source bootstrap reads are at most 64 MiB, and fresh complete private output is
at most 16 MiB. Preparation and apply compute separate conservative invoices
from actual whole-file lengths before writing. Namespace sizes are exact in
both manifests, including current entry/helper/guards and a 512-byte reserve.
This package's Source bound is a local finite invoice, not a new global rule.

Root has not executed any entry or controls merely because these files exist.

Synthetic-control qualification
--------------------------------

The controls call production bank validators, snapshot/prefix readers, cache-key
checks, projector, raw preservation checks and late CAS reader using explicitly
synthetic fixtures in a temporary directory. They never call prepare or apply.
They do not dynamically exercise the complete published-ledger authority chain
or every descriptor join. Those remain complete Source-review and independent
actual-plan-review duties. No fixture status, authority, descriptor or output
is reusable as evidence for an Original case. Controls cannot demonstrate
filesystem crash atomicity. Both entries and all controls are currently unrun.

The full conservative Source namespace includes both entries, the literal
helper, both supervisor files and reserve. Its exact byte count is in the
manifests; its local read namespace bound is 131,072 bytes. This is independent
of the 64 MiB total tracked-plus-bootstrap metadata read cap.
